#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1203
msgid "Mobile Cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1203
msgid "Serve cached pages to smartphones and tablets. When disabled, WordPress dynamically generates every page for mobile visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1204
msgid "Separate Mobile Cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1204
msgid "For themes that output different HTML for desktop and mobile. Maintains separate cache files per device type. Not needed for responsive themes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1205
msgid "Logged-in User Cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1205
msgid "Serve cached pages to logged-in users. SECURITY WARNING: all logged-in users and anonymous visitors share one cached copy of each page, so a page generated for one user — including their admin bar, nonces, or any user-specific content — can be served to other users and to the public. Only enable on sites that serve byte-for-byte identical content to everyone (e.g. membership sites with no per-user output)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1206
msgid "Gzip Compression"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1206
msgid "Pre-compress cache files with gzip. Supported browsers receive the compressed version, reducing transfer size by 60-80%. Recommended for most environments."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1207
msgid "Brotli Compression"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1207
msgid "Enable Brotli compression via mod_brotli (Apache 2.4+). Brotli achieves 15-25% better compression than gzip. Requires mod_brotli and .htaccess Optimization to be enabled. Falls back to gzip via mod_deflate if Brotli is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1208
msgid ".htaccess Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1208
msgid "Write optimization rules to .htaccess. Apache serves cached files directly without invoking PHP, significantly improving response time. Also enables mod_deflate compression and ETag removal. mod_expires and Cache-Control headers are added when \"Enable Browser Cache Headers\" is also on. No effect on Nginx."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1209
msgid "Cache 404 Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1209
msgid "Cache 404 (Not Found) pages. Reduces server load from repeated requests to non-existent URLs. The cached 404 page is served with proper 404 HTTP status code via the PHP drop-in. Note: .htaccess Optimization does not serve cached 404 pages (they always go through PHP to ensure the correct status code). Each unique missing URL creates its own cache entry, so on sites exposed to random-URL scans this can grow disk usage; expired entries are removed by the hourly cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1210
msgid "Mixed HTTP/HTTPS Site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1210
msgid "Enable only if your site intentionally serves both http:// and https:// versions of the same URL. When disabled (recommended), the cache scheme follows your Site Address setting — safe and tamper-proof. Reverse proxies are auto-detected. When enabled, the drop-in falls back to per-request header detection; sites behind a reverse proxy must also define PRIME_CACHE_TRUST_X_FORWARDED_PROTO in wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1211
msgid "Cache Footprint"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1211
msgid "Append an HTML comment with cache generation time to the source. Useful for verifying cache behavior via \"View Source\". Can be disabled in production."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1216
msgid ".htaccess Active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1217
msgid ".htaccess Not Writable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1224
msgid "Nginx Direct Serving (PHP-less)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1224
msgid "Nginx detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1226
msgid "Show the nginx configuration snippet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1227
msgid "On nginx, .htaccess has no effect, so every cached page still boots PHP before the cache file is read. Pasting this snippet into the server block of your nginx site configuration lets nginx serve Prime Cache files directly from disk — response time (TTFB) typically drops from 100-300 ms to a few milliseconds. The snippet reflects your current settings; copy it again after changing cache settings. After editing, run \"nginx -t\" and reload nginx. If you cannot edit the nginx configuration (shared hosting), this optimization is not available — the PHP drop-in keeps working as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1238
msgid "Enable Browser Cache Headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1238
msgid "Add Cache-Control and Expires headers to cached responses, both using the lifetimes configured below. HTML Cache-Control is applied by the PHP drop-in. CSS, JS, image, font, and Expires headers require .htaccess Optimization to be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1239
msgid "Immutable Cache-Control"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1239
msgid "Add \"immutable\" directive to Cache-Control for CSS, JS, images, and fonts. Tells the browser the file will never change during its lifetime, preventing conditional revalidation requests (304 checks)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1243
msgid "CSS & JS Cache Lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1244
msgid "Images / Media / Documents Cache Lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1245
msgid "Fonts Cache Lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1246
msgid "HTML Cache Lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-admin-settings.php:1246
msgid "0 = no-cache (recommended for HTML). Non-zero values cache HTML in the browser."
msgstr ""

